      ],
      "question": "Given that y = 1 at x = 0, solve the differential equation dy/dx = 6xy^(1/3)/e^(2x), y >= 0, giving your answer in the form y^2 = g(x).",
      "status": "ready",
      "answer": "y^2 = (2 - (2x + 1)e^(-2x))^3.",
      "steps": [
        "Separate the variables: y^(-1/3) dy = 6x e^(-2x) dx.",
        "The left side integrates to (3/2)y^(2/3).",
        "Integrate the right side by parts: integral of 6x e^(-2x) dx = -3x e^(-2x) - (3/2)e^(-2x) + C.",
        "Use y = 1 at x = 0: 3/2 = -3/2 + C, so C = 3.",
        "Multiply by 2/3: y^(2/3) = 2 - (2x + 1)e^(-2x).",
        "Cube both sides after squaring: y^2 = (2 - (2x + 1)e^(-2x))^3."
      ],
      "images": [
