      "question": "Find the particular solution of the differential equation dy/dx = 4y^2/sqrt(4x + 5), x > -5/4, for which y = 1/3 at x = -1/4, giving your answer in the form y = f(x).",
      "status": "ready",
      "answer": "y = 1/(7 - 2 sqrt(4x + 5)).",
      "steps": [
        "Separate: y^(-2) dy = 4(4x + 5)^(-1/2) dx.",
        "Integrate: -1/y = 2 sqrt(4x + 5) + C.",
        "At x = -1/4, 4x + 5 = 4, so sqrt = 2; with y = 1/3: -3 = 2(2) + C, so C = -7.",
        "So -1/y = 2 sqrt(4x + 5) - 7.",
        "Hence y = 1/(7 - 2 sqrt(4x + 5))."
      ],
