      "question": "The depth H metres of water in a tank satisfies dH/dt = -(H - 5)(H + 3)/40, where t is in days. Given H = 13 when t = 0, solve the differential equation to show that H = (10 + 3e^(-0.2t))/(2 - e^(-0.2t)).",
      "status": "ready",
      "answer": "H = (10 + 3e^(-0.2t))/(2 - e^(-0.2t)).",
      "steps": [
        "Separate: dH/((H - 5)(H + 3)) = -dt/40.",
        "Using part (a): (1/8)[ln|H - 5| - ln|H + 3|] = -t/40 + C.",
        "So ln((H - 5)/(H + 3)) = -t/5 + D; at t = 0, H = 13 gives (H - 5)/(H + 3) = 8/16 = 1/2.",
        "So (H - 5)/(H + 3) = (1/2)e^(-0.2t). Write E = e^(-0.2t).",
        "Rearrange: 2(H - 5) = E(H + 3), so H(2 - E) = 10 + 3E.",
        "Hence H = (10 + 3E)/(2 - E)."
      ],
      "images": [
        "papers/maths/img/P4-04-Differential-Equations-2.jpg",
        "papers/maths/img/P4-04-Differential-Equations-3.jpg"
      ]
