      "question": "The temperature theta degrees C of a car engine t minutes after it is turned off satisfies dtheta/dt = -k(theta - 15)^2, where k is a constant. The temperature is 85 C when the engine is turned off and 40 C exactly 10 minutes later. Solve the differential equation to show that theta = (at + b)/(ct + d), where a, b, c and d are integers.",
